    "title": "FTP server turns back on after being switched off, closing the app, and reopening it",
    "observed_behavior": "On the FTP server screen, if the user switches the FTP server off, closes Material Files from recents, reopens the app, and returns to the FTP server screen, the FTP server restarts on its own.",
    "expected_behavior": "After the user switches the FTP server off, closes the app, and re-opens it, the FTP server should remain off rather than turning back on by itself.",
    "steps_to_reproduce": "1. Open Material Files. <aa09f6aef3409759f67d672c9efcbd64d8f3b0ee61cf3e8d197f0539e34430d2>\n2. On the storage permission prompt, tap \"Allow\". <9253ef287211a96261d15d2522d1499f880b411f5e49851b98bae34f3403ab9d>\n3. Open the navigation drawer. <3abd760d81519f7d0b2fe5daa74c918b40f9496bef2bf776dd7b0d8e95a47b49>\n4. Tap \"FTP server\" in the navigation drawer. <ed4ddd149d2da1bda9c6a957048313602988bce3f183bd199efeacece662aeec>\n5. On the FTP server screen, tap the switch labeled \"OFF\" to switch the FTP server off. <5f369cd30bd1e5644d294c31e5ff58277cad40b2633f69cc4105944721df8b1b>\n6. Press back to leave the app to recents. <944abf1e97748f2436418aea5aa65a35e80ea307f807f0264ae85d2c80188e7c>\n7. Dismiss the Material Files task from recents. <b05234dc13810ef197b494fe9ce3b3d6e6927d53c722ad904f3dc53e425da84c>\n8. From the home screen, open the app drawer by tapping \"Apps\". <04cd15cb46f30016a649cd8febd12f4b4b097da6d72b65dd82dc5ae35e514b84>\n9. Tap \"Files\" to reopen Material Files. <8038deffe8ddbc1d6b34be696460e6ecac4b733c9b28d52f7e21cd0fd6d3a1f9>\n10. Open the navigation drawer again. <3abd760d81519f7d0b2fe5daa74c918b40f9496bef2bf776dd7b0d8e95a47b49>\n11. Tap \"FTP server\" to return to the FTP server screen. <ed4ddd149d2da1bda9c6a957048313602988bce3f183bd199efeacece662aeec>"
